# Connect Website to Admin Login & Panel

The public website's **Admin** button and the [public/admin/index.html](file:///c:/Users/KiTE/Downloads/staticpollachi/public/admin/index.html) redirect page both link to `http://localhost:5173` — the Vite dev server. This works only when the dev server is running, and breaks when the site is opened as a static file or deployed. 

The fix is to **build** the React admin app into `public/admin-app/` (a subfolder of the website) so it can be accessed with a simple relative link.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Admin App — Vite Build Config

#### [MODIFY] [vite.config.js](file:///c:/Users/KiTE/Downloads/staticpollachi/admin/vite.config.js)
Set `build.outDir` to `../public/admin-app` so `npm run build` drops the compiled files directly inside the public website folder.

```diff
 export default defineConfig({
   plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],
   base: './',
+  build: {
+    outDir: '../public/admin-app',
+    emptyOutDir: true,
+  },
 })
```

---

### 2. Public Website — Admin Nav Link

#### [MODIFY] [index.html](file:///c:/Users/KiTE/Downloads/staticpollachi/public/index.html)
Change the **Admin** button in the navbar from the hardcoded localhost URL to the built app's relative path:

```diff
-<a href="http://localhost:5173" target="_blank" class="btn btn-admin-nav" id="admin-portal-link" ...>
+<a href="admin-app/index.html" class="btn btn-admin-nav" id="admin-portal-link" ...>
```

---

### 3. Public Website — Admin Redirect Page

#### [MODIFY] [admin/index.html](file:///c:/Users/KiTE/Downloads/staticpollachi/public/admin/index.html)
Update the meta-refresh and manual link to point to the built app instead of localhost:

```diff
-<meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url=http://localhost:5173" />
+<meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url=../admin-app/index.html" />
 ...
-<a href="http://localhost:5173">Open Admin Panel →</a>
+<a href="../admin-app/index.html">Open Admin Panel →</a>
```

---

### 4. Run the Build

After the config change, run `npm run build` inside the `admin/` folder to produce `public/admin-app/`.

---

### 5. Admin "Back to Website" Link

The Login page already has `href="../index.html"` which will correctly navigate back to the public site once the admin is served from `public/admin-app/`.

